L861 patches for LineageOS 16.0 (Android 9)
===========================================

Run from the root of the LineageOS 16.0 source tree:

    sh device/openstone/L861/patches/check.sh      # dry run, changes nothing
    sh device/openstone/L861/patches/install.sh    # core set
    sh device/openstone/L861/patches/uninstall.sh  # git reset --hard + clean
                                                   # in every patched project

Optional sets are added by name:

    sh device/openstone/L861/patches/install.sh video
    sh device/openstone/L861/patches/install.sh video fmradio

All three sets were applied in order, with these scripts, to the LineageOS
lineage-16.0 branches of the patched projects. Nothing here has been
compiled or booted yet.

Core set (needed to build and boot)
-----------------------------------
Origin: "L861" = carried over unchanged from the 15.1 set of this tree,
"hermes" = taken from the lineage-16.0 device tree of the Xiaomi Redmi Note 2
(same MT6795 SoC, MTK Android M blobs).

  bionic
    0001 bionic-mtk-patch                         L861   export __pthread_gettid for the blobs
  frameworks/av
    0001 Disable-vndk-for-omx                     hermes
    0002 mediatek-Port-AV-changes                 hermes MTK OMX decode/encode basics (ACodec)
    0003 Disable-usage-of-get_capture_position    L861
  frameworks/base
    0001 Hardware-bitmaps-support-workaround      hermes
    0002 zygote-Add-ged-to-whitelisted-paths      hermes /proc/ged fd inherited by zygote
  frameworks/native
    0001 Do-not-use-presentOrValidate             hermes HWC1 behind the HWC2-on-1 adapter
    0002 Ignore-usage-bits-verification           hermes old gralloc usage bits
  frameworks/opt/telephony
    0001 add-mtk-ril-requests-unsol-responses     hermes same 50 lines as the 15.1 L861 patch
  hardware/interfaces
    0001 HWC2On1Adapter-Fix-fence-leak            hermes
    0002 Workaround-for-MTK-camera-blobs          L861
    0003 Lower-the-requirement-of-sensor-API...   L861
  system/core
    0001 liblog-Add-__xlog_buf_printf             L861
    0002 libsuspend-readd-earlysuspend            hermes replaces the 15.1 early_suspend patch
    0003 gatekeeperd-Add-use-software-gatekeeper  L861
  system/netd
    0001 Don-t-fail-on-FTP-conntracking-failing   hermes
    0002 Accept-broken-rpfilter-match             hermes kernel has no IPv4 rpfilter match

optional-video (enable after testing playback/recording on the device)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
  frameworks/av      YUV color profiles, HEVC enhancement, OMX decoder crop
                     info, MTK media profiles (hermes)
  frameworks/native  YUV color profiles header (goes with the av one)
The L861 OMX blobs are different builds from the hermes ones, so these are
not known to be needed, or correct, here.

optional-fmradio
----------------
  packages/apps/FMRadio  Suppress-compiler-warnings (hermes)
Note that both packages/apps/FMRadio and this tree's MTK_FM-RADIO define a
module named libfmjni.

Not carried over from 15.1 (kept under lineage-15.1/ for reference)
-------------------------------------------------------------------
  frameworks/av   libaudiohal LEGACY_MTK_AV_BLOB, libmedia MTK stubs: do not
                  apply to 16.0; hermes runs the same class of audio blob with
                  no audio patch. Re-port only if audio fails.
  frameworks/av   AutoscaleOmx: 16.0 has TARGET_OMX_LEGACY_RESCALING natively.
  hardware/interfaces  audio error-message suppression (2): do not apply.
  hardware/ril    BOARD_PROVIDES_RILD: replaced by ENABLE_VENDOR_RIL_SERVICE
                  in BoardConfig.mk.
  system/core     early_suspend: replaced by the hermes one.
  system/core     O-change-patch: its MTK ifc_* helpers now live in
                  hal/libril/libnetutils.c; the init ENV[] enlargement is not
                  carried over.
  telephony       RIL.java: replaced by the hermes port.

Deliberately not taken from hermes
----------------------------------
  frameworks/av MTK-camera-support: this tree provides the MTK camera
  parameters through its own libcamera_client_mtk.
  frameworks/base 0010: signature spoofing, unrelated to the port.
  bionic (2): the hermes install script does not apply them either; one
  does not apply to 16.0, the other reads a phh-specific property.
